---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/astro/Breadcrumb.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../../components/astro/CtaBanner.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Gibraltar Property Tracker Method" description="The proposed methodology for a Gibraltar property tracker: separate asking and achieved prices, identify sources and periods, disclose sample sizes and suppress unsupported results." type="article" updatedTime="2026-11-08">
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Market', href: '/market/' }, { label: 'Methodology' }]} />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[1000px] px-5 pb-20 pt-10 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-16">
    <p class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-sea-700">Proposed measurement rules</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink-900 sm:text-6xl">How a future Gibraltar property tracker should work</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-xs text-stone-600">Published 8 November 2026 · This is a proposal, not a report of current market conditions.</p>
    <p class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-terra-600/25 bg-white p-6 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-600">No verified current private-market dataset has been supplied. This page defines the evidence and disclosure required before prices, transaction counts, time-on-market measures or rental yields appear. It does not contain current statistics.</p>
    <div class="article-content mt-10">
      <h2 id="separate-the-measures">Keep asking prices separate from achieved prices</h2>
      <p>An asking-price series describes advertised offers observed during a stated collection period. It does not establish the amount a buyer ultimately paid. An achieved-price series should be published only when a completed transaction, consideration amount and date are verified from an appropriate source. The two series should never be merged into one “market price” figure.</p>
      <h2 id="name-sources">Name the source and explain coverage</h2>
      <p>Every release should identify source providers, the dates on which records were collected, the covered period, property types and locations represented, the share of records with missing fields and any permissions or usage limits. A provider feed can omit properties; the page should not say it covers “all Gibraltar” unless that is demonstrated. Official and advertised data measure different things and should be described separately.</p>
      <h2 id="deduplicate">Deduplicate and handle changes consistently</h2>
      <p>Where permission allows, compare listing references, normalized location details, size, bedrooms, price and dates to identify possible duplicates. Repeated adverts and simple text edits should not count as new homes in a snapshot. Record real price changes as listing history. Mark uncertain matches for review rather than silently counting them as separate evidence.</p>
      <h2 id="definitions">Define each metric before calculating it</h2>
      <p>Use the median for a stated observation set and show the record count, period and unit. Price per square metre requires a consistent, verified internal-area measure. “Days on market” needs a defined start and end event, plus dated listing history. A rental yield calculation would need relevant rents matched to comparable property values and a clear gross or net definition. Do not estimate a yield by dividing a few advertised rents by unrelated asking prices.</p>
      <h2 id="suppression">Suppress weak or incomparable segments</h2>
      <p>Set sample thresholds before viewing results. The tracker proposal is to suppress breakdowns with fewer than ten observations and to use a rolling twelve-month period where a quarterly sample is too small, while still displaying the period and sample count. These are proposed rules and do not guarantee that a sample represents the wider market. If records are insufficient, say “insufficient verified data.”</p>
      <h2 id="updates">Update only after a documented review</h2>
      <p>A future release could use calendar quarters and publish after source and duplicate checks. The page should record the publication date, the reporting period, methodology version, any revisions and what changed. Comparisons need consistent definitions and coverage. If a comparison cannot be supported, omit it rather than attribute a movement to policy, interest rates, supply or buyer behaviour without evidence.</p>
      <h2 id="download">Publish downloadable data only when rights allow</h2>
      <p>A CSV should include a plain-language data dictionary, units, source/coverage notes, time period and suppression markers. It should not include precise property addresses or personal information. Do not publish a download until the source licences or permissions allow reuse and each field can be explained.</p>
      <h2 id="limitations">Current limitations</h2>
      <p>No listing feed, complete historical listing file or verified private sale-price dataset is connected to this first release. There is no current chart, dataset download, price estimate, median or yield. Read the <a href="/market/property-price-tracker/">price tracker status</a> for the evidence available and the <a href="/market/quarterly-market-update/">quarterly update policy</a> for future reporting requirements.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10 border-t border-stone-200 pt-6 text-xs leading-6 text-stone-600">This methodology is an editorial proposal, not investment, legal, tax, lending or valuation advice. No statistic on this page represents current Gibraltar prices.</p>
    <div class="mt-8"><CtaBanner light eyebrow="Buyer resources" title="Compare what you can verify." description="Explore area guides and purchase information without treating an unsupported market estimate as a valuation." href="/guides/" label="Browse buyer guides" /></div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
